      "writtenOn": "2021-05-11T00:00:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While this comment is accurate and I see nothing particularly wrong with it (hence +2), I think it would be weird to heavily insist further on the possibility there are multiple wifis or cell concurrently at the same time. It\u0027s not like this is new in S ; many OEMs had multiple WiFis releases ago, and there are often multiple cell networks active at the same time (say, IMS \u0026 data), not to mention DS-DS devices that existed as far back as gingerbread.\nSo I don\u0027t think there is much to highlight there. It might be new to the stock WiFi stack, but for the connectivity stack and/or for some OEM wifi stacks, this is Android L, maybe even earlier.",
      "parentUuid": "8d033c6e_6a9af283",
